# Everything the build does not need, and two things it must never receive.
#
# `.env` is the first: the Makefile keeps real credentials there, and a build
# context that carries it puts them in an image layer where `docker history`
# reads them back. gitleaks watches the repository, not the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The second is `build/` -- a host build directory copied in would shadow the
# one the container produces, and `COPY --from=build /src/build/libs/*.jar`
# would ship whatever happened to be on the developer's machine.
build/
.gradle/
out/
bin/

.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

docs/
scripts/
*.md
!README.md

# The LaTeX image builds from its own context (docker/latex) and is a separate
# service in compose; it has no business in this one.
docker/
